  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Some words change their meaning just with a written accent. **Cuánto** and **cuanto** are a pair like that."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Form",
            "Job",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "cuánto, cuánta, cuántos, cuántas",
              "direct questions",
              "¿Cuántas olas agarraste?"
            ],
            [
              "",
              "indirect questions",
              "Dime cuánta sal le pongo."
            ],
            [
              "",
              "exclamations",
              "¡Cuánta gente!"
            ],
            [
              "cuanto (no accent)",
              "relative / connector",
              "cuanto antes, en cuanto llegues, cuanto más… más"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Cuánto** with an accent always carries the idea of _how much / how many_. As an adjective it agrees with the noun: **cuánto tiempo**, **cuánta sal**, **cuántos libros**, **cuántas películas**. It can also stand alone as a pronoun: **¿Cuántas?**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Indirect questions keep the accent even without question marks: **me pregunto cuánta gente habrá**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Without the accent, **cuanto** works as a connector or relative: **cuanto antes** (_as soon as possible_), **en cuanto** (_as soon as_), **cuanto más… más** (_the more… the more_), **todo cuanto** (_all that_)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: if you could say _how much_ or _how many_, it gets the accent."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
